WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.080
Hey, welcome to 40 Days of Holiness. Grab your workbook.

2
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.880
You know what to do, right? We're going to take notes.

3
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.020
We're going to work through all this.

4
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.280
Today's theme, let's see, we are on, oh goodness, day

5
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.350
10 today. Holiness means purity from

6
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:22.220
corruption.

7
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.000
You ever seen the yin-yang symbol, right?

8
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.820
It's like this universal symbol in Eastern religions.

9
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.561
The basic idea is that there's dark and light balance in the

10
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.340
universe, and that in all light there is some dark, in all dark there is some

11
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:36.720
light.

12
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.540
Eastern thinkers basically came to this

13
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.120
conclusion studying the universe, and that it's kind of a,

14
00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.160
honestly, natural conclusion to come to, right?

15
00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.180
There's some good in all bad, there's some bad in all good.

16
00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.290
Everything in the universe has its yin and its yang, some good, some bad, some

17
00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.660
corruption, but in the corruption, there's some purity, and in the strength,

18
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.520
there's some weakness, in some dark, in some light.

19
00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:01.740
Everything's mixed,

20
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.480
and the two are entangled. And that mixture includes

21
00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:07.619
moral corruption.

22
00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:12.120
So this can be in our actions like stealing, lying, and murder, and sometimes

23
00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.620
that's in the life of a relatively good person in other areas. Here's the thing.

24
00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.580
Yin and yang does not adequately explain the universe.

25
00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:22.700
It doesn't. Here's why. Because God's not mixed.

26
00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:26.800
He is utterly, unimaginably pure, completely incorruptible.

27
00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.460
So when God calls us to be holy like he's holy, he's

28
00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.820
requiring us to be untouched by that which

29
00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.940
brings corruption. So God

30
00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.960
talks about this kind of holiness in Leviticus, and he makes it a

31
00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:45.520
violation of his holiness to be touched by dead body or have an

32
00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.510
infection or touched by an unclean animal.

33
00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:52.120
And if we want to know God, we have to be free from evil actions, free

34
00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:56.060
from the guilt of sin. So Isaiah 59:2 says,

35
00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.160
"But your iniquities have separated you from God.

36
00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:03.000
Your sins have hidden his face from you so that he will not hear."

37
00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:07.620
But the corruption of sin goes deeper than just the actions that verse is talking

38
00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.480
about. It goes down into motivations, too.

39
00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.620
So this is why Jesus' teachings were so revolutionary.

40
00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.280
He taught in such a way that he exposed the heart of

41
00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:22.220
people. When he taught, he showed it was possible to do even

42
00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.680
right things from wrong motives.

43
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.800
There's lie mixed with honesty, or

44
00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.960
ambition, which is good, right, mixed with greed.

45
00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.320
There is selflessness that's mixed with selfish motive.

46
00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.700
Jesus even taught that there could be

47
00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.500
giving mixed with pride

48
00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.570
or arrogance mixed with prayer.

49
00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:45.109
In other words,

50
00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.640
even good actions can be mixed with morally

51
00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:51.800
corrupting motivations and influence.

52
00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.320
Now, the New Testament has many pictures of this, like Ezekiel

53
00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:00.320
14:4 says this: "Therefore, speak to them and tell them

54
00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.020
this is what the Sovereign Lord says.

55
00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:06.160
When any of the Israelites set up idols in their

56
00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:10.049
hearts, the Lord will answer them in keeping with

57
00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:13.790
their great idolatry." In other words, he's saying it's not just an idol in the

58
00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:17.390
corner of your house. The problem is that the idol got out of the corner of your

59
00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.460
house and got into your heart.

60
00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.000
Isaiah 6 talks about it as an issue of lips.

61
00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:26.120
Isaiah says, "I'm a man of unclean lips." And this becomes really

62
00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:30.130
important when you remember that in the New Testament, Jesus talks about

63
00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:33.020
it as the heart and the mouth together.

64
00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:36.260
Out of the overflow of the heart, the mouth speaks.

65
00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.560
So Isaiah's problem showed up in his mouth, but it came from his

66
00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:44.540
heart, even though he was right with God and was literally God's

67
00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:45.080
prophet.

68
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.560
Now David talks about it this way in Psalm 51:5.

69
00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:52.760
"Surely I was sinful at birth, sinful from the

70
00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.040
time my mother conceived me."

71
00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:59.760
And then he goes on to ask God to cleanse him with

72
00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.720
hyssop. Now, in Leviticus, in the Old Testament, hyssop was used

73
00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:07.680
in the purification ceremony for when you had come into contact with a

74
00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:10.400
dead body or leprosy, something that defiled you.

75
00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:14.900
So before you could come back into the holy place, into the presence of

76
00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.769
God, the temple or tabernacle, you had to be sprinkled with

77
00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.460
hyssop, symbolically cleansing you from the

78
00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:25.600
potential corruption of being unclean.

79
00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:30.180
So put this together. David's saying this corruption that's inside

80
00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:35.020
is like being present from the time I was born and before, is

81
00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.700
like being continually in contact with a dead body.

82
00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:41.280
I need to be sprinkled so I can come back into the presence of God.

83
00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.040
It keeps me continually stuck in the outer levels of holiness.

84
00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.360
I can't come to the middle, to the center where God is.

85
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:52.620
David's like, "This internal corruption's keeping me from

86
00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:55.390
journeying deep into God's essential nature.

87
00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:59.500
It keeps me from really getting into him and knowing him."

88
00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.180
It's the same for me and you.

89
00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:05.860
Now, tomorrow, we're going to look more at this nature of what it's like.

90
00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:07.940
I will give you a brief word of warning here.

91
00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:11.340
We're going into a few hard days, okay? Buckle up.

92
00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.070
We're going to look in the mirror. We're going to talk about some uncomfortable

93
00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:18.080
realities. We're going to clean out the wound so it

94
00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:18.500
can heal.

95
00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.620
All right? You know you got to do that, right?

96
00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:23.220
Sometimes you got to clean out the wound before it can heal.

97
00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:23.680
But listen,

98
00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:27.000
God can heal the wound of the heart.

99
00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.880
Don't get discouraged by the clean-out process.

100
00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:33.480
Don't get discouraged by the fact that we've got to dive in deep and figure out

101
00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:36.800
what the problem is all the way down to the core.

102
00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:40.790
It's not enough to just play around the edges and say, "I'm going to clean up some

103
00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.560
of these public things in my life and do holier stuff."

104
00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:48.320
God says, "I want to dive down deep and transform not just the actions on the

105
00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:52.140
outside, but the motivations of the heart." So

106
00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:55.660
let's do that, all right? Let's go deep with the Lord, and

107
00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.360
be willing to stick with me for the next few days.

108
00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.040
I promise it's going to get more encouraging.

109
00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.320
The next few days, you're going to look inside and say,

110
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.860
"I see what's here, and I see where there's corruption.

111
00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:10.880
I see where there's negative things, and I want God to clean it out."

112
00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.420
All right? So stick with me. Do the workbook.

113
00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:17.200
Let's stay with it for the next few days, and God's going to heal some things, some

114
00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:20.880
really deep stuff in your heart and in our hearts. All right? God bless you.

115
00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:21.510
See you tomorrow.
